# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trivenix Partners — Environment Variables Reference
# Reference only. Store credentials in Replit Secrets.
# Never commit real credentials or a populated .env file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database (Neon PostgreSQL) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Add the pooled connection string as NEON_DATABASE_URL in Replit Secrets.
NEON_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# ── Session ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-secret

# ── First Admin Bootstrap (one-time setup) ──────────────────────────────────
# Set these to create the initial admin account. After first login, change the
# password and unset/remove these variables.
ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL=your-admin-email@example.com
ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-secure-password

# ── CORS (production API server only) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of allowed frontend origins.
# Example: https://yourapp.vercel.app,https://yourdomain.com
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourapp.vercel.app,https://yourdomain.com

# ── Email / SMTP ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Use Gmail SMTP with a Google App Password (not your normal Gmail password).
# Enable 2-Step Verification on the Google account, then generate an App Password.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your-company@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your-gmail-app-password
SMTP_FROM="Trivenix Partners <your-company@gmail.com>"
ADMIN_EMAIL=your-company@gmail.com

# ── AI Assistant (Google Gemini) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-only. Never expose in VITE_ variables or the browser.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# ── Media Storage (Cloudinary) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. If not configured, admins can still add YouTube/Vimeo/external
# video URLs as a fallback. File uploads will be unavailable.
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your-cloudinary-cloud-name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your-cloudinary-api-key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your-cloudinary-api-secret

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Replit Quick-Start
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Add environment values in Replit Secrets. Use NEON_DATABASE_URL for Neon;
#    this takes precedence over a runtime-provided DATABASE_URL.
#
# 2. The imported Neon database already has the app schema and data. For a new,
#    empty database only, run:
#      pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push
#      pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server exec tsx src/scripts/seed.ts
#
# 3. Start application uses `pnpm dev`: API on port 8080 and frontend on port 5000.
#    The frontend proxies /api requests to the API server.
#
# 4. Create an admin only if the database has no admin account. Set
#    ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL and ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD, then call
#    POST /api/admin/bootstrap or run bootstrap-admin.ts.
#
# 5. Verify /api/healthz, public services, SMTP connection, Gemini chat, and
#    Cloudinary credentials. The admin email test sends a real message.
